@@ -48,6 +49,25 @@ If you'd rather run the Docker image yourself, you can read more about that in t
 > that people have someone to contact if they need help with their account. If that bothers you, put in any
 > email address you want and create yourself a new admin account.
 
+## Chat bots
+
+Open **Account settings** and choose **Set up chat bots** to create a bot and copy
+its bot code. The code is a secret credential: anyone with it can post as that bot
+to rooms where the bot is a member. The full raw request body becomes the message:
+
+```sh
+curl --data-binary "Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅" \
+  https://chat.example.com/rooms/<room-id>/<bot-code>/messages
+```
+
+Bots only join rooms selected for them by default. Enable **Add to all open rooms**
+to add a bot to every current and future open room. Set its optional **Webhook URL**
+to receive a JSON callback whenever someone mentions it or first adds it to a
+room. Direct conversations do not send this callback. The webhook is delivered
+in a background job. A `200` response with a `text/plain` or
+`text/html` content type is posted as the bot; a `204` response posts nothing.
+Bots can also use the `reply_to` URL in the callback to post later.
+
 ## Development
 
 You are welcome - and encouraged - to modify Campfire to your liking.
